---
// How it works, in three steps along one line. Each step has its own drawing, animated in CSS (the
// third also with SMIL motion paths); with reduced motion asked for, every drawing shows still.
---
<section id="how" class="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <div class="wrap inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">HOW IT WORKS</p>
    <h2 id="how-title">Three steps, then it runs on its own.</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li data-reveal>
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
        <div class="text">
          <h3>Save what the code can't show</h3>
          <p class="lead">Tell the agent, or let DD ask after a fix. A memory names the files, symbols or commands it applies to, and why reading the code would not reveal it.</p>
          <p class="tag">SAVED WITH EVIDENCE</p>
          <p class="fact">DD hashes the file the memory cites. Verified evidence activates it at once; anything else waits for you in the review UI.</p>
        </div>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 440 260" role="img" aria-label="A file of the repository is linked to a new memory, which gets a verified seal">
          <path d="M38 96h46l18 18v84a8 8 0 0 1-8 8H38a8 8 0 0 1-8-8V104a8 8 0 0 1 8-8Z" fill="#0f1318" stroke="#2b333d" stroke-width="2" />
          <path d="M84 96v18h18" fill="none" stroke="#2b333d" stroke-width="2" />
          <rect x="44" y="130" width="40" height="6" rx="3" fill="#2b333d" />
          <rect x="44" y="146" width="30" height="6" rx="3" fill="#2b333d" />
          <rect x="44" y="162" width="36" height="6" rx="3" fill="#2b333d" />
          <path class="link" d="M110 150 C 140 150, 140 130, 168 130" fill="none" stroke="#e8b84a" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4 6" />
          <rect x="168" y="44" width="200" height="176" rx="18" fill="#12161c" stroke="#2b333d" stroke-width="2" />
          <rect class="grow" x="190" y="68" width="56" height="14" rx="7" fill="#e8b84a" style="animation-delay: 0.2s" />
          <rect class="grow" x="190" y="100" width="150" height="8" rx="4" fill="#3a434f" style="animation-delay: 0.5s" />
          <rect class="grow" x="190" y="118" width="124" height="8" rx="4" fill="#3a434f" style="animation-delay: 0.7s" />
          <rect class="grow" x="190" y="136" width="96" height="8" rx="4" fill="#3a434f" style="animation-delay: 0.9s" />
          <rect class="grow" x="190" y="170" width="104" height="26" rx="13" fill="rgba(143,198,255,0.12)" stroke="#8fc6ff" stroke-width="1.5" style="animation-delay: 1.2s" />
          <circle class="grow" cx="206" cy="183" r="4" fill="#8fc6ff" style="animation-delay: 1.4s" />
          <rect class="grow" x="216" y="180" width="60" height="6" rx="3" fill="#8fc6ff" opacity="0.7" style="animation-delay: 1.4s" />
          <g class="seal">
            <circle cx="362" cy="52" r="24" fill="#0b0d10" stroke="#5fd08a" stroke-width="3" />
            <path class="tick" d="M351 52l8 8 14-16" pathLength="1" fill="none" stroke="#5fd08a" stroke-width="3.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
          </g>
        </svg>
      </li>
      <li data-reveal>
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
        <div class="text">
          <h3>DD matches every action</h3>
          <p class="lead">Before each read, edit or command, a hook checks the triggers compiled from your memories.</p>
          <p class="tag">RULES, NOT SEARCH</p>
          <p class="fact">A rule matches or it doesn't. Only matches are delivered.</p>
          <p class="tag">LOCAL</p>
          <p class="fact">No account, no model calls, no background process, no dependencies.</p>
        </div>
        <svg class="first" viewBox="0 0 440 260" role="img" aria-label="Tool calls flow through a gate; only the one that matches a trigger lights up">
          <line x1="20" y1="130" x2="420" y2="130" stroke="#1d232b" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="2 8" stroke-linecap="round" />
          <rect x="200" y="62" width="40" height="136" rx="20" fill="rgba(232,184,74,0.05)" stroke="#e8b84a" stroke-width="2" />
          <circle class="burst" cx="220" cy="130" r="22" fill="none" stroke="#e8b84a" stroke-width="2" />
          {[0, 1.2, 2.4, 3.6, 4.8].map(delay => (
            <circle class:list={['dot', { match: delay === 2.4 }]} cx="20" cy="130" r="9" fill="#3a434f" style={`animation-delay: ${delay}s`} />
          ))}
        </svg>
      </li>
      <li data-reveal>
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
        <div class="text">
          <h3>The agent gets it in time</h3>
          <p class="lead">The memory arrives with the tool call it applies to, once per session. A session that never touches those files never pays for it.</p>
          <p class="tag">SHARED THROUGH GIT</p>
          <p class="fact">Memories are JSON files in your repository. A teammate who pulls gets the same deliveries, and reviews new memories like code.</p>
        </div>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 440 260" role="img" aria-label="From the repository, a memory travels to the two teammates whose work it applies to, and not to the third">
          <path id="route-a" d="M104 130 C 200 130, 220 56, 334 56" fill="none" stroke="#2b333d" stroke-width="2" />
          <path id="route-b" d="M104 130 C 200 130, 240 130, 334 130" fill="none" stroke="#2b333d" stroke-width="2" />
          <path d="M104 130 C 200 130, 220 204, 334 204" fill="none" stroke="#2b333d" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="3 7" />
          <circle cx="78" cy="130" r="28" fill="rgba(232,184,74,0.1)" stroke="#e8b84a" stroke-width="2" />
          <circle cx="70" cy="122" r="4" fill="none" stroke="#e8b84a" stroke-width="2" />
          <circle cx="70" cy="140" r="4" fill="none" stroke="#e8b84a" stroke-width="2" />
          <circle cx="88" cy="128" r="4" fill="none" stroke="#e8b84a" stroke-width="2" />
          <path d="M70 126v10M84 129c-6 1-10 4-12 9" fill="none" stroke="#e8b84a" stroke-width="2" />
          {/* Each packet and the teammate it reaches share one SMIL clock (same begin and dur): the packet
              arrives at 40% of the cycle and is absorbed, and the teammate lights up at that moment. */}
          {[{ route: 'route-a', y: 56, begin: '0s' }, { route: 'route-b', y: 130, begin: '0.8s' }].map(({ route, y, begin }) => (
            <Fragment>
              <g class="teammate">
                <circle class="node" cx="356" cy={y} r="22" fill="#12161c" stroke="#2b333d" stroke-width="2">
                  <animate attributeName="stroke" values="#2b333d;#2b333d;#e8b84a;#e8b84a;#2b333d" keyTimes="0;0.4;0.43;0.9;1" dur="4s" begin={begin} repeatCount="indefinite" />
                  <animate attributeName="fill" values="#12161c;#12161c;#2a2416;#2a2416;#12161c" keyTimes="0;0.4;0.43;0.9;1" dur="4s" begin={begin} repeatCount="indefinite" />
                </circle>
                <circle class="head" cx="356" cy={y - 6} r="6" fill="#3a434f">
                  <animate attributeName="fill" values="#3a434f;#3a434f;#e8b84a;#e8b84a;#3a434f" keyTimes="0;0.4;0.43;0.9;1" dur="4s" begin={begin} repeatCount="indefinite" />
                </circle>
                <path class="body" d={`M346 ${y + 10}c2-6 18-6 20 0`} fill="none" stroke="#3a434f" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round">
                  <animate attributeName="stroke" values="#3a434f;#3a434f;#e8b84a;#e8b84a;#3a434f" keyTimes="0;0.4;0.43;0.9;1" dur="4s" begin={begin} repeatCount="indefinite" />
                </path>
              </g>
              <circle class="packet" r="6" fill="#e8b84a" opacity="0">
                <animateMotion dur="4s" begin={begin} repeatCount="indefinite" keyPoints="0;1;1" keyTimes="0;0.4;1" calcMode="linear"><mpath href={`#${route}`} /></animateMotion>
                <animate attributeName="opacity" values="1;1;0;0" keyTimes="0;0.4;0.44;1" dur="4s" begin={begin} repeatCount="indefinite" />
              </circle>
            </Fragment>
          ))}
          <circle cx="356" cy="204" r="22" fill="#0b0d10" stroke="#222a33" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="3 5" />
          <circle cx="356" cy="198" r="6" fill="#222a33" /><path d="M346 214c2-6 18-6 20 0" fill="none" stroke="#222a33" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        </svg>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .how { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-1); }
  .inner { max-width: 1200px; padding-top: 96px; padding-bottom: 96px; }
  .eyebrow { margin: 0; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
  h2 { margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 38px); line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.025em; color: var(--text-strong); font-weight: 600; }
  /* One gold line runs through the numbers, fading out after the last. */
  .steps { margin: 56px 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 140px;
    background: linear-gradient(#e8b84a, rgba(232, 184, 74, 0.35) 50%, rgba(232, 184, 74, 0)) no-repeat 19px 20px / 2px calc(100% - 40px); }
  li { position: relative; padding-left: 72px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 40px; }
  .num { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 40px; height: 40px; display: grid; place-items: center; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--bg); border: 2px solid var(--accent); color: var(--accent); font: 600 15px var(--font-mono); }
  .text { flex: 1 1 340px; min-width: 0; }
  h3 { margin: 4px 0 10px; font-size: 26px; letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: var(--text-heading); font-weight: 600; }
  .lead { margin: 0; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .tag { margin: 20px 0 0; font: 500 12px var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent); }
  .tag + .fact + .tag { margin-top: 16px; }
  .fact { margin: 4px 0 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text); }
  svg { flex: 1 1 420px; min-width: 0; max-width: 520px; height: auto; }
  /* The middle step draws on the left, so the drawings zigzag. */
  svg.first { order: -1; }

  .grow { transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: left center; animation: grow 4.8s ease infinite both; }
  @keyframes grow { 0% { transform: scaleX(0); opacity: 0; } 12% { transform: scaleX(1); opacity: 1; } 88% { opacity: 1; } 100% { opacity: 0; } }
  .link { stroke-dashoffset: 60; animation: link 4.8s ease infinite; }
  @keyframes link { 0% { opacity: 0; stroke-dashoffset: 60; } 10% { opacity: 1; } 30%, 90% { stroke-dashoffset: 0; opacity: 1; } 100% { opacity: 0; } }
  .seal { transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: center; animation: seal 4.8s cubic-bezier(0.2, 1.5, 0.4, 1) infinite; }
  @keyframes seal { 0%, 40% { transform: scale(0) rotate(-30deg); opacity: 0; } 50% { transform: scale(1.15) rotate(0); opacity: 1; } 56%, 90% { transform: scale(1); opacity: 1; } 100% { opacity: 0; } }
  /* The tick draws itself once the seal has landed. Its length is 1 (pathLength) and the gap after the dash
     is longer than the path, so nothing shows before it draws; it stays invisible until then, since a round
     cap would otherwise leave a dot where the stroke starts. */
  .tick { stroke-dasharray: 1 2; stroke-dashoffset: 1; opacity: 0; animation: tick 4.8s ease infinite; }
  @keyframes tick { 0%, 52% { stroke-dashoffset: 1; opacity: 0; } 53% { opacity: 1; } 66%, 100% { stroke-dashoffset: 0; opacity: 1; } }
  .dot { transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: center; animation: travel 6s linear infinite; opacity: 0; }
  @keyframes travel { 0% { transform: translateX(0); opacity: 0; } 6% { opacity: 1; } 94% { opacity: 1; } 100% { transform: translateX(400px); opacity: 0; } }
  .dot.match { animation-name: travel-match; }
  @keyframes travel-match {
    0% { transform: translateX(0); opacity: 0; fill: #3a434f; } 6% { opacity: 1; }
    46% { transform: translateX(184px) scale(1); fill: #3a434f; } 50% { transform: translateX(200px) scale(1.6); fill: #e8b84a; }
    62% { transform: translateX(248px) scale(1.3); fill: #e8b84a; } 94% { opacity: 1; fill: #e8b84a; }
    100% { transform: translateX(400px) scale(1.3); opacity: 0; fill: #e8b84a; }
  }
  .burst { transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: center; opacity: 0; animation: burst 6s ease-out 2.4s infinite; }
  @keyframes burst { 0%, 48% { transform: scale(0.6); opacity: 0; } 50% { transform: scale(0.8); opacity: 1; } 64% { transform: scale(2.2); opacity: 0; } 100% { opacity: 0; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .grow, .link, .seal, .tick, .dot, .burst { animation: none; opacity: 1; transform: none; stroke-dashoffset: 0; }
    .dot { opacity: 0; } .dot.match { opacity: 1; fill: #e8b84a; transform: translateX(200px); }
    .packet { display: none; }
    /* CSS outranks the SMIL-animated attributes: still, the two teammates it reaches are lit. */
    .teammate .node { stroke: #e8b84a; fill: #2a2416; }
    .teammate .head { fill: #e8b84a; }
    .teammate .body { stroke: #e8b84a; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .inner { padding-top: 64px; padding-bottom: 64px; }
    .steps { margin-top: 40px; gap: 72px; background-position: 15px 16px; background-size: 2px calc(100% - 32px); }
    li { padding-left: 52px; gap: 24px; }
    .num { width: 32px; height: 32px; font-size: 13px; }
    h3 { font-size: 22px; margin-top: 2px; }
    .text, svg { flex-basis: 100%; }
    /* Stacked, every step reads text first, drawing second. */
    svg.first { order: 0; }
  }
</style>
